# FOOTWORK DRILLS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Footwork Drills are structured movement exercises designed to improve locomotion, positioning, balance, acceleration, deceleration and movement efficiency during combat.

Within CAS, they are considered one of the highest-transfer neuromotor exercises for all combat sports.

---

# Philosophy

Power is useless if it cannot be delivered.

Technique is useless if positioning is poor.

Excellent footwork allows athletes to create angles, control distance and maximize the effectiveness of every offensive and defensive action.

CAS selects Footwork Drills whenever improving movement quality is a primary objective.

